From 3cba8566173841e7f981db42a5d90a86b0296240 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:49:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 144/274] DeepSeek V4.1 prefill SP: Engram's exchanged blocks
 read in place

The all-to-all of Engram's wkv product padded each rank's [T, C] block to
the SP row count and the receiver copied the blocks into packed rows: two
copies of about 69 MB a call on TP3 (roughly 10 ms of a 16K prefill).

The collective is now a row-block all-to-all (all_to_all_rows): rank r
receives every rank's rows [r * L, r * L + real) of its block, real being
its real rows, so no padding is sent or copied; the result is [N, L, C].
The TileLang gate reads those column blocks in place
(engram_gate_blocked: the same loads in the same order, logical column c
at block c // C, column c % C; C is a multiple of the vector width, so no
vector straddles two blocks), with the same bits as the packed gate. The
B12X mix still takes packed rows (pack_columns, one copy).

Tests: the blocked gate's bits equal the packed gate's at TP3's and TP4's
block widths, masked and not, with rows past the tokens NaN; every rank
receives every rank's block of its real rows and packs them into its rows
of the gathered product.

